# Push = git push + Vercel production deploy

When the user asks to **push** changes (or ship / release / put live), do **all** of the following from the repo root:

1. Commit if there are uncommitted changes (follow the normal commit protocol).
2. `git push` to the remote.
3. Deploy production with the Vercel CLI: `npx vercel --prod`
4. Confirm the production URL (project `testament-bible-learning` → https://testament-bible-learning.vercel.app).

Never treat `git push` alone as done. Do not skip the Vercel prod step unless the user explicitly says not to deploy.
